  "id": "Compound::DB01029 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Irbesartan is likely to interact with Cyp2c9 through a shared pathway involving Cyp2c8. The evidence suggests that Irbesartan binds to Cyp2c8, which then participates in oxidoreductive activities, such as those acting on chiral or ch2 groups, or arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity. These activities are all mediated by Cyp2c9, indicating a potential functional link between Irbesartan and Cyp2c9. The overlapping roles of Cyp2c8 in different enzymatic activities imply that Irbesartan may influence Cyp2c9 through a common intermediary, possibly by modulating the activity of Cyp2c8. This mechanism highlights a potential regulatory relationship where Irbesartan could affect Cyp2c9 via a shared metabolic pathway, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
